From 5b313e84d645cfb8cc62469f8967b70def332687 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: My Naai <dev@mynaai.in>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:29:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Page headers lose their subtitle, and every button holds its
 own label
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two things reported from a phone, fixed together because both are the same
complaint: the panel spends screen space on words and then draws the remaining
words outside the boxes they belong to.

Subtitles are gone from the four pages that had one — Booking requests
("Customer enquiries, salon answers and missed leads. Opens on today (IST)…"),
Notifications, Plans & Trials and Shop Settings. Each one restated what the
control underneath it already said, and each one cost a full row above the fold
on a phone. The filter card's "Search, filter and page through every request"
line went with them; the tab title and the field labels still say it.

Buttons now wrap their own label instead of spilling past the rounded edge:
`min-width: 0` so a flex row can shrink them, `overflow-wrap: anywhere` for a
single long word, and a slightly smaller label on phones. "Accept for salon" and
"Decline for salon" in the request footer, and "Send Notification" in the
Notifications composer, were the ones running out of their card.
---
 src/index.css                   | 42 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/pages/BookingRequests.jsx   |  9 ++++---
 src/pages/PlansAndTrials.jsx    |  8 +++----
 src/pages/PushNotifications.jsx | 13 +++++-----
 src/pages/ShopSettings.jsx      |  8 +++----
 5 files changed, 58 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/index.css b/src/index.css
index 7f8cf92..29230b9 100644
--- a/src/index.css
+++ b/src/index.css
@@ -2718,4 +2718,44 @@ img {
     height: 35px;
     font-size: 13px;
     margin-top: 3px;
-}
\ No newline at end of file
+}
+/* ── Button labels stay inside their button ─────────────────────────────────
+   Reported from a phone: a label longer than the button it sits in was drawn
+   past the rounded edge — and in the Booking requests cards and the detail
+   modal's footer it ran out of the card entirely. A button now wraps its own
+   text instead of refusing to: the box grows a line taller, the words never
+   leave it. `min-width: 0` is what lets a flex row (`.d-flex` footers, the
+   mobile action grids) actually shrink the button rather than push the row
+   wider than the screen, and `overflow-wrap: anywhere` covers one long word.
+   The `.text-nowrap` utility still wins where a label really must not break. */
+.btn {
+  min-width: 0;
+  max-width: 100%;
+  white-space: normal;
+  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
+  text-align: center;
+  line-height: 1.25;
+}
+.btn > svg,
+.btn > i {
+  flex: 0 0 auto;
+}
+.btn-group > .btn,
+.d-flex > .btn {
+  flex-shrink: 1;
+}
+
+/* On a phone the label drops a notch and the padding tightens, so a sentence
+   like "Accept for salon" keeps one line inside a two-column footer. */
+@media (max-width: 575.98px) {
+  .btn {
+    font-size: 0.82rem;
+    padding-left: 0.7rem;
+    padding-right: 0.7rem;
+  }
+  .btn-sm {
+    font-size: 0.78rem;
+    padding-left: 0.6rem;
+    padding-right: 0.6rem;
+  }
+}
